#
#
#now getting into implementation details, if there are more than 5 input bits, then we will need to have more than 1 ROM, so 6 bits means 2 rom, 7 means 4 roms

#use logic on the OE line to drive the correct rom out. if only one rom is needed, always output. 
#if there are more than 64 output bits, use 2 ROMs with the same OE signal and aissng accordingly

#so if there are 7 inpput bits and 70 output bits, we need i think 8 ROM in total
